 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No sea, drowning or destruction drawn. Which land is meant in 137:6-11 is not glossed (Al-Muyassar: Syria; As-Sa'di: Egypt). Light for «وتمت كلمت ربك الحسنى». First-person «فانتقمنا… فأغرقناهم… دمرنا» not used. STAGING v4: c1 (136): Pharaoh and his army are never drawn and no body is shown: an empty sea shore by day (As-Sa'di quotes their pursuit at sunrise; not dawn, not night); an hourglass for the appointed time of their end (136:1, gloss), the water rises over the empty shore on 136:3 and a wave plate stands for the sea (136:5-8). c2 (137): the people who had been oppressed (an uncountable people, men and women) walk into a blessed farmland: fields that turn green on 137:10 (Al-Muyassar: blessed with crops, fruits and rivers). Which land is meant is not drawn (Al-Muyassar: Syria; As-Sa'di: Egypt): a generic farmland, no landmark. A seal plate for the fulfilled good promise of the Lord (137:12-18). Pharaoh's buildings are not drawn: a brick-wall plate appears on what they made (137:24) and its lines retract (undraw) on 137:29, for the destruction of what they built; nothing falls on the people."
 },
